One historical demonstration for flip_cup_collect_cookies, episode 4640. Reference instruction: Flip the cup so that the opening faces upward, then pour all the cookies into the bowl.
Arm roles: Both arms for cup reorientation and handover; the right arm subsequently lifts and pours the plate.
Observed sequence: The left hand picks up the inverted cup and rotates it sideways. The right hand receives it while the left hand opens and withdraws, then sets the cup down with its opening upward. The right hand next grasps the cookie plate at its rim, brings a low edge over the bowl, and progressively tilts the plate so cookies fall into the bowl. Return and release the empty plate. The cup and receiving bowl are distinct objects.
Visual outcome: The cup remains opening-up on the table, the plate is visibly empty, cookies are visible in the bowl, and both hands withdraw.
Evidence limits: No official success label or exact final cookie count is available. Transfer the handover and pouring geometry; the reference's absolute positions and durations are not live commands.
